1
00:00:00,065 --> 00:00:01,589
November 2008.

2
00:00:01,964 --> 00:00:04,230
Nariman House, Mumbai.

3
00:00:04,648 --> 00:00:06,901
Two gunmen are holding a Jewish centre,

4
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:09,531
and commandos are about to come down the

5
00:00:09,544 --> 00:00:10,169
stairs.

6
00:00:11,451 --> 00:00:13,261
On a phone line from Pakistan,

7
00:00:13,886 --> 00:00:15,761
a calm voice gives them an order.

8
00:00:16,178 --> 00:00:18,274
Pile the mattresses at the top of the

9
00:00:18,287 --> 00:00:18,912
stairs.

10
00:00:19,329 --> 00:00:20,813
Wait for the commandos.

11
00:00:21,991 --> 00:00:24,322
Six hostages died in that building.

12
00:00:24,739 --> 00:00:27,160
Among them were a rabbi and his wife.

13
00:00:27,577 --> 00:00:27,968
Later,

14
00:00:28,489 --> 00:00:29,921
according to court testimony,

15
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,447
a friend of the plotters compared the man

16
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,478
on the phone to one of history's great

17
00:00:34,491 --> 00:00:35,103
generals.

18
00:00:36,349 --> 00:00:38,576
The compliment was passed along to him.

19
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,755
The man on the phone was never in the

20
00:00:41,768 --> 00:00:42,224
room.

21
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,477
His name is Sajid Mir,

22
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:47,484
and the FBI calls him the chief planner of

23
00:00:47,498 --> 00:00:48,630
26/11.

24
00:00:49,047 --> 00:00:51,443
Since then, Pakistan has described him as

25
00:00:51,456 --> 00:00:54,060
free, as dead, and — for one very

26
00:00:54,073 --> 00:00:56,026
convenient season — as a convict.

27
00:00:57,275 --> 00:00:59,397
So where is the man who ran Mumbai by

28
00:00:59,410 --> 00:00:59,905
phone?

29
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:02,537
And why has no court ever tried him for

30
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:02,810
it?

31
00:01:03,991 --> 00:01:06,166
Everything here comes from the FBI's 

32
00:01:06,179 --> 00:01:07,090
wanted notice,

33
00:01:07,546 --> 00:01:10,072
sworn testimony in a Chicago courtroom,

34
00:01:10,502 --> 00:01:12,871
and Pakistan's own court order.

35
00:01:14,216 --> 00:01:16,794
His status, it turns out, changes whenever

36
00:01:16,807 --> 00:01:17,862
someone needs it to.

37
00:01:25,270 --> 00:01:27,640
He was born in Lahore in the mid-to-late

38
00:01:27,653 --> 00:01:28,760
1970s.

39
00:01:29,163 --> 00:01:31,104
Records disagree on the year.

40
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:34,189
His father ran a small textile business.

41
00:01:34,606 --> 00:01:37,249
Mir studied English literature and Islamic

42
00:01:37,262 --> 00:01:39,658
studies at the University of the Punjab.

43
00:01:40,075 --> 00:01:42,249
He married a retired army officer's

44
00:01:42,262 --> 00:01:42,692
daughter,

45
00:01:43,265 --> 00:01:44,489
and they had two sons.

46
00:01:45,761 --> 00:01:48,105
On paper, he could have been a mid-level

47
00:01:48,118 --> 00:01:49,016
civil servant.

48
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:51,221
That was the point.

49
00:01:51,637 --> 00:01:55,114
Inside Lashkar-e-Taiba, he rose to deputy

50
00:01:55,127 --> 00:01:57,132
head of international operations —

51
00:01:57,627 --> 00:01:59,775
in effect, its foreign desk.

52
00:02:00,166 --> 00:02:00,999
He didn't fight.

53
00:02:01,416 --> 00:02:02,275
He recruited.

54
00:02:02,796 --> 00:02:04,906
His speciality was people with the right

55
00:02:04,919 --> 00:02:05,700
passports,

56
00:02:06,156 --> 00:02:08,304
men who could cross a Western airport

57
00:02:08,317 --> 00:02:09,528
without a second look.

58
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:12,276
According to investigators, he had already

59
00:02:12,288 --> 00:02:15,062
run operatives into Virginia, Europe and

60
00:02:15,075 --> 00:02:16,611
Australia before Mumbai.

61
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:19,174
Some of them were caught.

62
00:02:19,578 --> 00:02:20,437
He never was.

63
00:02:21,844 --> 00:02:24,344
Before he sent anyone to Mumbai, he went

64
00:02:24,357 --> 00:02:25,047
himself.

65
00:02:25,464 --> 00:02:28,550
In 2005, according to investigators, Mir

66
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:30,516
entered India on a fake passport,

67
00:02:31,076 --> 00:02:33,680
posing as a fan at an India Pakistan

68
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,034
cricket match in Delhi.

69
00:02:35,438 --> 00:02:37,196
He stayed about fifteen days.

70
00:02:38,473 --> 00:02:40,322
Not all of them at the cricket.

71
00:02:40,739 --> 00:02:42,744
Part of that time, he spent looking at

72
00:02:42,757 --> 00:02:43,382
Mumbai.

73
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,643
Then he found a better pair of eyes.

74
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:49,169
David Headley — the man from our last

75
00:02:49,183 --> 00:02:51,253
file — became his operative, and Mir

76
00:02:51,253 --> 00:02:52,308
became his handler.

77
00:02:52,711 --> 00:02:53,948
He funded the trips.

78
00:02:54,352 --> 00:02:55,706
He chose the targets.

79
00:02:56,123 --> 00:02:58,258
Headley later testified that Mir kept

80
00:02:58,271 --> 00:02:59,599
pushing for more detail:

81
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,477
floor plans, routes, the layout of the

82
00:03:02,477 --> 00:03:02,985
Taj.

83
00:03:04,261 --> 00:03:05,641
Headley was the camera.

84
00:03:06,058 --> 00:03:08,154
Mir decided where it pointed.

85
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:11,191
When ten gunmen came ashore in

86
00:03:11,204 --> 00:03:14,212
November 2008, the man directing them had

87
00:03:14,225 --> 00:03:15,566
already walked the ground.

88
00:03:16,957 --> 00:03:19,613
For sixty hours, Mir sat in a control room

89
00:03:19,626 --> 00:03:21,606
in Karachi — the room from our second

90
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:22,061
file.

91
00:03:22,465 --> 00:03:24,366
He was on the phone to the gunmen.

92
00:03:24,783 --> 00:03:26,501
Indian news channels played on the

93
00:03:26,514 --> 00:03:29,379
screens, broadcasting where the commandos

94
00:03:29,392 --> 00:03:30,030
were moving.

95
00:03:31,278 --> 00:03:33,400
He was watching the same coverage as

96
00:03:33,414 --> 00:03:34,273
everyone else.

97
00:03:35,449 --> 00:03:37,715
The FBI's  wanted notice calls him the

98
00:03:37,728 --> 00:03:39,017
attack's "chief planner",

99
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:41,738
and "one of the key controllers during the

100
00:03:41,751 --> 00:03:42,350
attacks."

101
00:03:43,541 --> 00:03:46,302
At Nariman House, Headley later testified

102
00:03:46,315 --> 00:03:48,802
in Chicago, Mir told the two gunmen to

103
00:03:48,815 --> 00:03:50,872
barricade the stairs with mattresses and

104
00:03:50,885 --> 00:03:52,252
wait for the commandos.

105
00:03:52,669 --> 00:03:55,872
Tahawwur Rana, hearing about it, compared

106
00:03:55,885 --> 00:03:58,268
the tactic to Khalid bin Walid, a

107
00:03:58,281 --> 00:04:00,468
legendary seventh-century general.

108
00:04:00,859 --> 00:04:02,838
He asked Headley to pass the praise to

109
00:04:02,838 --> 00:04:03,242
Mir.

110
00:04:04,525 --> 00:04:07,077
Six hostages had died in that building.

111
00:04:07,468 --> 00:04:09,616
The compliment was delivered anyway.

112
00:04:11,024 --> 00:04:14,032
Headley was arrested in October 2009.

113
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:17,027
He told the FBI everything he knew about

114
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,769
his handler.

115
00:04:18,144 --> 00:04:21,100
He even helped agents try to lure Mir out

116
00:04:21,113 --> 00:04:22,077
of Pakistan.

117
00:04:23,368 --> 00:04:24,540
Mir didn't come.

118
00:04:25,901 --> 00:04:27,477
He didn't need to hide, either.

119
00:04:27,852 --> 00:04:30,951
Zabiuddin Ansari, a Lashkar operative

120
00:04:30,964 --> 00:04:33,308
later arrested by India, told

121
00:04:33,321 --> 00:04:35,652
investigators that Mir twice visited

122
00:04:35,665 --> 00:04:38,594
Zaki-ur-Rehman Lakhvi in Adiala Jail, in

123
00:04:38,607 --> 00:04:39,519
Rawalpindi.

124
00:04:39,925 --> 00:04:42,359
Lakhvi was Lashkar's operations chief,

125
00:04:42,958 --> 00:04:44,508
then on trial for Mumbai.

126
00:04:44,938 --> 00:04:47,542
On the second visit, in September 2009,

127
00:04:47,737 --> 00:04:50,159
Lakhvi reportedly told the men around him

128
00:04:50,172 --> 00:04:51,878
he had "struck a deal with the

129
00:04:51,891 --> 00:04:52,464
government."

130
00:04:52,867 --> 00:04:54,586
No more arrests would follow.

131
00:04:55,776 --> 00:04:57,664
A year later, Indian counter-terror

132
00:04:57,677 --> 00:05:00,099
officials say, Mir was planning his next

133
00:05:00,112 --> 00:05:00,503
strike:

134
00:05:01,206 --> 00:05:04,083
the police academy at Nashik, north-east

135
00:05:04,096 --> 00:05:04,774
of Mumbai.

136
00:05:05,149 --> 00:05:06,230
It never happened.

137
00:05:07,507 --> 00:05:09,538
But this was not a man on the run.

138
00:05:10,924 --> 00:05:14,010
In April 2011, a federal grand jury in

139
00:05:14,023 --> 00:05:16,198
Chicago indicted him — conspiracy,

140
00:05:16,211 --> 00:05:18,268
material support to terrorists, the

141
00:05:18,281 --> 00:05:20,156
killing of US citizens abroad.

142
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,669
The United States offered up to five

143
00:05:22,682 --> 00:05:24,843
million dollars for information leading to

144
00:05:24,856 --> 00:05:25,195
him.

145
00:05:25,586 --> 00:05:28,307
The FBI says he may since have had plastic

146
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:28,945
surgery.

147
00:05:30,228 --> 00:05:32,559
The face on the poster may no longer be

148
00:05:32,572 --> 00:05:33,067
his.

149
00:05:34,214 --> 00:05:35,816
Then, quietly, he died.

150
00:05:36,191 --> 00:05:37,571
At least, on paper.

151
00:05:37,990 --> 00:05:40,477
Pakistan let its partners understand that

152
00:05:40,477 --> 00:05:41,376
Mir was dead,

153
00:05:41,961 --> 00:05:43,524
without ever confirming it.

154
00:05:43,928 --> 00:05:46,154
Western governments asked for proof.

155
00:05:47,398 --> 00:05:48,114
None came.

156
00:05:48,531 --> 00:05:50,432
The US State Department's terrorism

157
00:05:50,445 --> 00:05:50,914
report,

158
00:05:51,461 --> 00:05:53,518
released in December 2021,

159
00:05:54,156 --> 00:05:56,552
still described him as believed to remain

160
00:05:56,565 --> 00:05:57,021
free.

161
00:05:58,191 --> 00:05:59,025
Dead to some.

162
00:05:59,428 --> 00:06:00,444
Free to others.

163
00:06:01,675 --> 00:06:03,576
It depended on who was asking.

164
00:06:04,957 --> 00:06:07,327
Then someone started asking who mattered.

165
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,675
The Financial Action Task Force is the

166
00:06:10,688 --> 00:06:13,031
global watchdog on terror financing.

167
00:06:13,461 --> 00:06:15,922
It had kept Pakistan on its grey list

168
00:06:15,935 --> 00:06:19,099
since 2018, and its next key review was

169
00:06:19,112 --> 00:06:21,456
due in Berlin in June 2022.

170
00:06:22,588 --> 00:06:25,700
In April 2022, the dead man was

171
00:06:25,713 --> 00:06:26,403
arrested.

172
00:06:27,677 --> 00:06:30,320
Weeks later, on May 16, an

173
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:32,495
anti-terrorism court convicted him.

174
00:06:32,898 --> 00:06:33,901
Not for Mumbai.

175
00:06:34,318 --> 00:06:36,050
For financing terrorism.

176
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:38,784
Fifteen and a half years, across three

177
00:06:38,797 --> 00:06:39,526
sentences.

178
00:06:39,902 --> 00:06:42,454
The trial was held behind closed doors,

179
00:06:42,792 --> 00:06:45,240
inside Lahore's Kot Lakhpat Jail.

180
00:06:45,633 --> 00:06:46,779
No reporters.

181
00:06:47,182 --> 00:06:48,419
No announcement.

182
00:06:48,836 --> 00:06:49,826
According to Dawn,

183
00:06:50,346 --> 00:06:52,378
the verdict surfaced only weeks later,

184
00:06:52,951 --> 00:06:54,695
through court papers and lawyers.

185
00:06:55,881 --> 00:06:58,199
Pakistan put the conviction in front of

186
00:06:58,212 --> 00:06:59,006
the watchdog.

187
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:00,943
It worked.

188
00:07:01,362 --> 00:07:03,966
That October, Pakistan came off the grey

189
00:07:03,979 --> 00:07:04,500
list.

190
00:07:05,672 --> 00:07:07,456
Dead while nobody was asking.

191
00:07:07,873 --> 00:07:10,620
Alive, arrested and convicted in the weeks

192
00:07:10,646 --> 00:07:12,209
a regulator needed proof.

193
00:07:13,493 --> 00:07:15,811
And never once tried for the attack that

194
00:07:15,824 --> 00:07:17,764
killed 166 people.

195
00:07:19,170 --> 00:07:21,332
With a conviction on file, the United

196
00:07:21,345 --> 00:07:23,793
States and India asked the UN Security

197
00:07:23,806 --> 00:07:26,319
Council to list Mir as a global terrorist.

198
00:07:26,722 --> 00:07:29,196
That would mean an asset freeze, a travel

199
00:07:29,209 --> 00:07:30,915
ban and an arms embargo.

200
00:07:32,071 --> 00:07:34,115
China put the request on hold.

201
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:36,656
Then it did it again.

202
00:07:37,073 --> 00:07:39,508
It was a technical hold, a procedural

203
00:07:39,521 --> 00:07:41,891
brake that any permanent member can pull.

204
00:07:42,307 --> 00:07:43,284
In the same period,

205
00:07:43,896 --> 00:07:46,200
China used it on other Pakistan-based

206
00:07:46,213 --> 00:07:46,760
militants,

207
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,325
including Hafiz Saeed's son.

208
00:07:49,742 --> 00:07:51,773
India's diplomat at the UN said

209
00:07:52,281 --> 00:07:54,065
the pattern showed that something was

210
00:07:54,573 --> 00:07:56,344
"genuinely wrong with the global

211
00:07:56,357 --> 00:07:57,958
counter-terrorism architecture."

212
00:07:59,277 --> 00:08:01,933
So the man the FBI calls the chief planner

213
00:08:01,946 --> 00:08:04,564
of 26/11 stands convicted of a lesser

214
00:08:04,577 --> 00:08:06,439
crime, in a closed court.

215
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,126
As of the latest reporting,

216
00:08:09,582 --> 00:08:11,692
he is still not on the UN's  sanctions

217
00:08:11,704 --> 00:08:12,108
list.

218
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:16,315
In December 2023, reports

219
00:08:16,328 --> 00:08:18,671
surfaced in Pakistan and India.

220
00:08:19,064 --> 00:08:20,809
Mir had been poisoned inside

221
00:08:20,809 --> 00:08:22,749
Dera Ghazi Khan Central Jail,

222
00:08:23,348 --> 00:08:25,757
they said, and flown by the army to a

223
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:27,931
military hospital in Bahawalpur,

224
00:08:28,413 --> 00:08:29,272
on a ventilator.

225
00:08:29,689 --> 00:08:31,538
None of it has been confirmed.

226
00:08:31,955 --> 00:08:34,051
Indian intelligence sources suggested,

227
00:08:34,077 --> 00:08:35,939
without proof, that it might have been

228
00:08:35,952 --> 00:08:38,765
staged — a way to vanish before anyone

229
00:08:38,778 --> 00:08:39,963
could ask for him again.

230
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:44,176
Since then, nothing verified has surfaced.

231
00:08:45,447 --> 00:08:47,791
Alive or dead, in prison or free —

232
00:08:48,312 --> 00:08:50,603
as of the latest reporting, nobody outside

233
00:08:50,603 --> 00:08:51,840
Pakistan can say.

234
00:08:53,224 --> 00:08:55,633
Every other name in this story ended on

235
00:08:55,646 --> 00:08:56,323
the record.

236
00:08:56,727 --> 00:08:57,820
Headley took a plea.

237
00:08:58,237 --> 00:09:00,789
Rana was extradited to face trial.

238
00:09:02,023 --> 00:09:04,992
Sajid Mir's  record does something else.

239
00:09:05,369 --> 00:09:07,622
It opens and closes on command.

240
00:09:08,041 --> 00:09:09,786
Dead when that was convenient.

241
00:09:10,202 --> 00:09:12,858
Convicted when a regulator needed proof.

242
00:09:13,275 --> 00:09:15,931
Tried only for a crime that never required

243
00:09:15,944 --> 00:09:18,106
saying the word Mumbai in open court.

244
00:09:19,289 --> 00:09:21,997
In 2008 he was the voice in the room,

245
00:09:22,466 --> 00:09:24,563
giving orders to men he never stood

246
00:09:24,576 --> 00:09:25,162
beside.

247
00:09:26,436 --> 00:09:28,819
Years later, he is still only a voice.

248
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:31,475
And the room he spoke from has never been

249
00:09:31,488 --> 00:09:32,048
opened.
